# adversarial-shard-merge drives the merge and the siblings it resolves beside itself by name (lib.sh:33-38, :324-347),
# the provenance schema, and sources the shared preamble. Nothing enumerates core/scripts/, so the
# scripts are declared one by one, against a fresh sandbox read-set trace. validate-provenance-block.sh's optional
# probes -- lib/meta-gate.sh and core/skills/ai-dlc/extensions/known-skills.json -- do not exist at tip and are not declared.
!core/scripts/merge-adversarial-shards.sh
# The merge hands every marked shard to this sibling's --admit-marker (BL-750); absent, every marked arm refuses.
!core/scripts/content-seal.sh
core/scripts/partition-document.sh
core/scripts/partition-subject.sh
# The shipped-sequence arms DVRS/DVRSS run the worklist without --keep, which consumes the split's pre-repair snapshot (BL-911).
core/scripts/serial-remediation-worklist.sh
core/scripts/validate-adversarial-convergence.sh
core/scripts/validate-provenance-block.sh
core/scripts/validate-steering-budget.sh
core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh
# The real producer of a sealed `sha=` marker: the CS1 arm seals the reference sibling with its --mark (BL-974).
core/scripts/wait-for-deliverable.sh
core/schemas/provenance-block.json
# The shared fixture lib this fixture sources (run.sh:2 preamble.sh; lib.sh sources none), file by file: the whole
# directory keyed every push that touched an unrelated lib file.
core/fixtures/lib/preamble.sh
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
# The merge derives each shard dispatch id from the write ledger this hook appends; every shard the fixture writes drives it.
core/hooks/ai-dlc-gate-remediation-guard.sh
# The installed rulebook every derived-set world commits: the merge narrows only where it carries the validator's ERA_TOKEN (BL-911).
core/skills/ai-dlc/steps/_gate-procedures.md
# Shard d of adversarial-shard-merge (BL-1095): every input the parent declares, since the driver execs the parent's run.sh, which
# sources its lib.sh and seeds the same worlds; the parent's run.sh, lib.sh and seeds by name, because a fixture's OWN directory is copied by the runner
# and this shard's own is only the driver (README.md and the parent's decls are read by nothing the shard runs). Only shard c's derived-set unit (dv) consumes the installed rulebook, so only its decl requires it.
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/lib.sh
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/run.sh
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.192-ff-A-token-decimal-resolution.md
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.bug-192-il-accuracy.md
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.doc-serial-epics.md
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.doc-test-strategy.md
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.files-b3-merged.expected
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.finding-headings.txt
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge/seed.story-1-rebalancer-il-accuracy.md
# The shard drivers: the parent's coverage join reads every one (BL-1095). A fixture's OWN run.sh is copied by the runner itself.
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge-c/run.sh
core/fixtures/adversarial-shard-merge-d/run.sh
# The dist-only shards (b) are declared, and their drivers and markers checked, only by those shards: a consumer carries none of them, so this shipped shard declares none.
core/fixtures/lib/world.sh
